      "title": "Improper Input Validation in io.undertow:undertow-core",
      "description": "Affected versions of io.undertow:undertow-core are vulnerable to Improper Input Validation. The Undertow HTTP server core fails to properly validate incoming `Host` headers. An attacker who sends malformed or arbitrary Host values can poison HTTP caches, probe or scan internal network services, or hijack user sessions by exploiting Host-based routing or cookie binding.",
